# Collaboration Modes

Select the collaboration mode based on risk, ambiguity, and verification strength.

| Mode | Use when | Human effort | Agent effort |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| AI First | CRUD, scaffolding, template docs, clear localized fixes | 20% review | 80% execution |
| Human First | Business-critical logic, core algorithms, architecture, irreversible choices | 70% design | 30% support |
| Pair Mode | Refactoring, debugging, legacy analysis, exploratory prototypes | 50% | 50% |

Default to Pair Mode when uncertain.

## AI First Preconditions

- Scope is clear and bounded.
- Existing patterns are discoverable.
- Verification commands or manual acceptance criteria exist.
- No destructive data or infrastructure operation is required.

## Human First Triggers

- Architecture boundaries are unclear.
- Business rules are incomplete or disputed.
- Security, compliance, finance, identity, or data retention is involved.
- The change could lock in a long-term platform decision.

## Pair Mode Behavior

- Read and summarize relevant context first.
- Propose a small plan for multi-file work.
- Implement in narrow increments.
- Verify after each meaningful step when practical.

## Background or Parallel Work

Use background agents or parallel tasks only when the subtasks are isolated and can be verified independently. Keep write access scoped to the files required for the task.
